1. For packages, I want to keep the descriptions of the packages in the report, same with settings.
2. Also add a description column for the tactical settings in the report
3. Reduce the excessive vertical height of tables when imported into Word. Word wraps each cell's text in its default "Normal" paragraph style (~8pt space-after, 1.08x line spacing), inflating every row. Fix in the report CSS by zeroing paragraph margins and pinning line-height (e.g. p/td/th margin:0, line-height:1.05) and trimming cell padding slightly.
4. Fix the document sitting too far to the right / feeling cramped. The body margin (24pt) doesn't set Word's page margins; Word keeps its own 1-inch page margins and adds the 24pt on top as an extra indent. Fix by controlling the page box explicitly (@page margin:1in) and setting body margin to 0.
5. Set report fonts: headings in Arial Bold, regular/body text in Arial. Declare font-family explicitly per element (h1/h2 = Arial bold, body/td/th/p = Arial) rather than relying on cascade, since Word reapplies its own theme fonts to cells and headings.